cademy-id "q-106324" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\frac{2}{x+5}=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $x=-5$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the left-hand side zero.\n\nWe can flip an equation involving two fractions as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{d}{c}\n$$\n\nThe above technique works whenever $a$ and $c$ are both different from zero.\n\nTherefore, we can flip the given equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+5}{2}=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nThe above equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+5}{2}=4\n$$\n\nWe can now solve this equation using the multiplication and the addition principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{x+5}{2}\\right) & =2\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{x+5}{\\cancel{2}}\\right) & =8 \\\\ x+5 & =8 \\\\ x+5-5 & =8-5 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce4cf6fe-52ce-57e9-b242-0bd13032b5ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce4cf6fe-52ce-57e9-b242-0bd13032b5ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce4cf6fe-52ce-57e9-b242-0bd13032b5ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-590c1066-c2b3-5f96-ae20-75e02640b2e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb5f206d-9010-556a-98c3-a48c71b9e1ce" "answer-8d01fb2b-91b3-5128-be1a-d928008aa632" "answer-590c1066-c2b3-5f96-ae20-75e02640b2e2" "answer-0c09cb2e-792c-5b50-9ddb-61b4ad09d949" "answer-f2f8fc4b-e975-5087-9d1f-ddd9534cddff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb5f206d-9010-556a-98c3-a48c71b9e1ce" :answer/id #uuid "eb5f206d-9010-556a-98c3-a48c71b9e1ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d01fb2b-91b3-5128-be1a-d928008aa632" :answer/id #uuid "8d01fb2b-91b3-5128-be1a-d928008aa632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-590c1066-c2b3-5f96-ae20-75e02640b2e2" :answer/id #uuid "590c1066-c2b3-5f96-ae20-75e02640b2e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c09cb2e-792c-5b50-9ddb-61b4ad09d949" :answer/id #uuid "0c09cb2e-792c-5b50-9ddb-61b4ad09d949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2f8fc4b-e975-5087-9d1f-ddd9534cddff" :answer/id #uuid "f2f8fc4b-e975-5087-9d1f-ddd9534cddff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1592a32d-005d-5261-a0e4-09fc6b72ccf5" :question/id #uuid "1592a32d-005d-5261-a0e4-09fc6b72ccf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-106322" :question/problem "Solve the equation $2=\\frac{7}{x+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $x=-3$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the right-hand side zero.\n\nWe can flip an equation involving two fractions as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{d}{c}\n$$\n\nThe above technique works whenever $a$ and $c$ are both different from zero.\n\nTherefore, we can flip the given equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{x+3}{7}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve this equation using the addition and the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{x+3}{7} \\\\ 7\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) & =7\\cdot \\left(\\frac{x+3}{7}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & =\\cancel{7}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{x+3}{\\cancel{7}}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & =x+3 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2}-3 & =x+3-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17ad2725-54e9-5e8e-9e65-216f8922f0e7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17ad2725-54e9-5e8e-9e65-216f8922f0e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "17ad2725-54e9-5e8e-9e65-216f8922f0e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76caab9b-0240-534e-af0e-2c